SPEC §3.1, CLI.md §2.3 (DECISIONS 332): --root wins over project.local.canon; placed where no directory is, the required root stops the command (E1013, exit 2).
-- dir --
p
-- args --
check
--root
src=../nowhere
-- p/project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
  roots {
    src: "../Source"
  }
}
-- p/project.local.canon --
project acme {
  roots {
    src: "../work/Source"
  }
}
-- work/Source/n.json --
3
-- want --
[exit 2]
[stdout]
error[E1013]
  root "src" ("../nowhere", from --root or Options.Roots) is not a directory on this machine: give an existing directory, or list the root in optional_roots in project.canon

1 error, 0 warnings in 0 packages (…)
